# PWKM Scripts Configuration
# Copy this file to .env, in this same directory, and fill in your values.
#
# Every variable below can be set here. The scripts load this file before they
# read any configuration, so a value set here takes effect everywhere.
#
# Precedence: a real environment variable WINS over anything in this file.
# That lets you override a single setting for one invocation without editing
# the file, for example:
#     set LOCAL_TIMEZONE=Asia/Tokyo && python date_utils.py --json now
#
# A missing .env is not an error. If you would rather configure everything
# through real environment variables, delete this file and set them there.
# Scripts that genuinely cannot run without a value say so by name.


# === Credentials ===

# Notion API key.
# Create an integration at https://www.notion.so/my-integrations and copy the
# "Internal Integration Secret". Grant that integration access to every
# database the scripts touch, not just the Tasks database. A missing grant
# looks exactly like an empty database rather than an error.
NOTION_API_KEY=your_notion_api_key_here

# Notion database ID for your Tasks database.
# Found in the database URL: https://notion.so/DATABASE_ID?v=...
# The 32-character string, with or without hyphens.
NOTION_DATABASE_ID=your_database_id_here

# Google Calendar OAuth credentials.
# Create a project at https://console.cloud.google.com/, enable the Google
# Calendar API, then create OAuth 2.0 credentials of type "Desktop app".
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id_here
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret_here


# === Settings ===

# Your timezone, as an IANA name. Used by every script that formats or
# compares times. If unset, the scripts fall back to North American Eastern,
# which is almost certainly wrong for you. Set this first.
LOCAL_TIMEZONE=America/New_York

# Path to the Python interpreter the startup script should use when invoking
# helper scripts. Defaults to whichever interpreter is running it, which is
# usually correct. Set it if it is not.
# PWKM_PYTHON=C:\Users\YOUR_USERNAME\AppData\Local\Programs\Python\Python3XX\python.exe

# Directory holding persistent state files (session timer, audit state) and
# the running-summaries subdirectory. Defaults to the parent of this scripts
# directory.
# PWKM_STATE_DIR=C:\path\to\your\pwkm\state

# Full path to the exported tasks CSV. Consulted only as a fallback: the
# scripts look beside themselves first, which is where the export lands by
# default. Set it if you keep the CSV somewhere else.
# PWKM_TASKS_CSV=C:\path\to\notion_tasks.csv

# Full path to the health database. Optional. Leaving it unset disables the
# health section of the startup report rather than causing an error.
# PWKM_HEALTH_DB=C:\path\to\health.db

# Comma-separated calendar IDs to merge into the calendar view alongside your
# primary calendar. Useful for a work calendar that exposes only free/busy.
# Leave unset for primary-calendar-only.
#
# Each entry may carry an optional display label, used to tag the merged
# events. Without one, the local part of the address is used.
#     PWKM_SECONDARY_CALENDARS=Work=you@work.example.com,family@example.com
# PWKM_SECONDARY_CALENDARS=you@work.example.com

# Weather section of the startup report. Leave the coordinates unset and the
# section skips cleanly rather than erroring.
#
# PROVIDER SUPPORT IS CANADA-ONLY at present: the only implemented provider is
# Environment Canada. Outside Canada, leave these unset.
# PWKM_WEATHER_LAT=43.65
# PWKM_WEATHER_LON=-79.38
# PWKM_WEATHER_LOCATION=Toronto, ON
# PWKM_WEATHER_PROVIDER=environment_canada

# Market section of the startup report. Set neither variable and the section
# skips cleanly. Requires the optional dependency yfinance.
#
# Entries are Label=Symbol. Symbols are whatever yfinance expects, so Toronto
# listings take a .TO suffix, and a ticker containing a dot uses a hyphen
# instead (Canadian Tire class A is CTC-A.TO but reads better as CTC.A).
# PWKM_MARKET_INDICES=S&P 500=^GSPC,Dow Jones=^DJI
# PWKM_PORTFOLIO_TICKERS=CTC.A=CTC-A.TO,NTR=NTR.TO
# PWKM_MARKET_THRESHOLD=2.0


# === Notes on format ===
#
# KEY=value                  plain
# KEY="value"                quotes are stripped
# export KEY=value           an export prefix is ignored
# KEY=value  # a comment     an unquoted trailing comment is stripped
#
# The file may be saved with or without a byte-order mark; both work.